{:edb/db-before-t 825 :edb/db-after-t 826 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534138 50 #inst "2026-10-06T04:11:37.416Z" 13194139534138 true] [17592186083136 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278285 13194139534138 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278292 13194139534138 true] [17592186083137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278299 13194139534138 true] [17592186083138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278306 13194139534138 true] [17592186083482 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534138 true] [17592186083482 1100 "$P(15,4)=$" 13194139534138 true] [17592186083482 1100 "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n$P(\\frac{15}{4}) =$" 13194139534138 false] [17592186083482 1145 "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(15,4)$ means the same thing as ${}_{15}{P}_{4}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(15,4) & =\\frac{15!}{(15-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{11!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot \\cancel{11!}}{\\cancel{11!}} \\\\  & =15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =32\\,760.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278286 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1089 "q-122228" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1100 "A store manager is choosing $3$ employees to do the morning, afternoon, and night shifts. If the store has $9$ employees and each can work a single shift, how many ways of choosing the $3$ employees does the manager have?" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1113 #uuid "389845c9-f18b-5fa8-a95e-85a428c5db03" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278285 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $9$ employees to choose from, so $n=9.$ We want to select $3$ of them for the three different shifts, so we have $r=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the number of different choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{9}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{9!}{(9-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9!}{6!} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7\\cdot \\cancel{6!}}{\\cancel{6!}} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 8\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =504.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278287 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278288 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278289 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278290 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278291 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1041 "selection" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278289 13194139534138 true] [17592186278286 1110 #uuid "5ee13080-4c4c-5d83-898a-bac9342f2917" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278287 1034 "60\\,480" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278287 1111 #uuid "d0100fe0-1a63-5601-9980-9bd0257d714f" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278288 1034 "3\\,024" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278288 1111 #uuid "8b82456e-abe5-566b-a3dc-b37a4eb5a9b3" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278289 1034 "504" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278289 1111 #uuid "93506760-ae07-5680-b5c0-68f32107e732" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278290 1034 "27" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278290 1111 #uuid "abe71e53-199e-54c6-af67-2843790566a3" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278291 1034 "729" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278291 1111 #uuid "8bbe531b-cbd2-506f-a601-5210d8cb4132" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278293 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1089 "q-122480" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1100 "A chocolate box has $15$ different chocolates. In how many ways can $5$ chocolates be eaten in a row?" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1113 #uuid "3a17faf1-2bcf-5207-a24d-54b14bb6a7d9" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278292 1145 "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $15$ chocolates, so $n=15.$ We want to select $5$ of those chocolates in a row so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of possible choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{15}{P}_{5} & =\\frac{15!}{(15-5)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15!}{10!} \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11\\cdot \\cancel{10!}}{\\cancel{10!}} \\\\  & =15\\cdot 14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12\\cdot 11 \\\\  & =360\\,360.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278294 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278295 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278296 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278297 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278298 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1041 "selection" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278295 13194139534138 true] [17592186278293 1110 #uuid "1225daf8-ecfa-5258-ac0b-5c5e375249fc" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278294 1034 "32\\,760" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278294 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278294 1111 #uuid "5ac9e41a-922a-59e1-bf55-81f088a42ae1" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278295 1034 "360\\,360" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [17592186278295 1111 #uuid "eed9cd0f-de0e-578f-8189-c191f172b824" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278296 1034 "24\\,024" 13194139534138 true] [17592186278296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534138 true] [175921862